title: The Party in Revolt
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dissent_percent >= 28 and month >= 1 and revolt_cooldown <= 0
priority: 450

= The Party in Revolt

Factional resentments have reached the breaking point. Leaders of several factions are airing grievances in public, donors are nervous, and the base is confused. Something must be done.

- @revolt_concede: Concede policy demands
- @revolt_unity: Make a high-profile unity push
- @revolt_purge: Reassert central control

@revolt_concede
on-arrival: revolt_cooldown = 18; progressive_dissent -= 6; moderate_dissent -= 6; labor_dissent -= 6; populist_dissent -= 6; abundance_dissent -= 6; establishment_dissent -= 6; budget -= 1

We buy peace by promising more than we can deliver.

@revolt_unity
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
on-arrival: revolt_cooldown = 18; progressive_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent -= 4; labor_dissent -= 4; populist_dissent -= 4; abundance_dissent -= 4; establishment_dissent -= 4; resources -= 1

A summit and a joint statement calm the waters.

@revolt_purge
on-arrival: revolt_cooldown = 18; establishment_strength += 6; establishment_dissent -= 10; progressive_dissent += 6; moderate_dissent += 4; left_relation -= 6; dem_enthusiasm -= 0.6

Order returns, at a price.
